SU>As far as I'm concerned, using backups of a game to prolong a game is
SU>only even remotely legit, IMHO, when it involves getting around file
SU>crashes, modem problems, and the like

    Using a backup file to prolong a game due to a crash is completely
legit in my book.

    As far as "idiot keystrokes", I would certainly give you your "put
all" in bag of holding, but how about if the default is deadly, and,
because your system is slow, you accidentally hit one return too many?
Now, some of us DON'T have all day, and can only get to play the game
during brief breaks.  If we had to carefully monitor every single
keystroke, we would NEVER be able to finish.  So we do a little
type-ahead.  Or we rely on touch-typing.  And, sometimes, the wrong key
gets hit, completely by accident (as opposed to "I forgot about the
wand of cancellation" type of accident; I am talking about hitting the
key next to the one you REALLY want to hit, so that your action is
radically different than the one you intended to use).

